{"body":"Canonical task: `O01` in [work-items.json](https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/blob/main/docs/restart/work-items.json).\n\nThis issue provides discussion and evidence links. Task state, dependencies and acceptance remain authoritative in Git; issue closure alone does not establish acceptance.\n\n- Convert the accepted operating model into concise repository instructions with one task-state authority.\n- Each task records scope, input/candidate commits, worktree ownership, acceptance and independently reviewed evidence.\n- Use Astra xhigh for requested hardware/security agents, isolated editing worktrees and one CAD writer.\n- Validate task dependencies and generated views; demonstrate resume from a fresh session without relying on chat memory.\n- Autonomy preserves existing authorization and respects concrete irreversible-action boundaries without repetitive confirmations.\n- Track readiness and release evidence separately for all active profiles; no global gate on an unrelated product.\n- Run the structural/evidence validator and negative tests in CI; demonstrate a fresh-session handoff and truthful resource availability. The check cannot verify physical measurements or replace substantive independent review.\n\nFollow [the development contract](https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/blob/main/docs/restart/development.md): reviewed specification, meaningful tests/experiments, bounded implementation, distinct exact-candidate review and affected integration gates. Preserve missing resources and failed observations.\n","number":7,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/nSealr/nsealr/issues/7"}
